---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="AI Receptionist Buyer's Guide — 5 Questions to Ask Before Buying | Birky Studio" description="A practical guide for real estate agents shopping for an AI receptionist. What to look for, what to avoid, and how much you should actually pay." image="/images/birky-mascot.jpg">

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0f172a 0%,#1e1b4b 50%,#312e81 100%);padding:100px 0 80px;position:relative;overflow:hidden;">
    <div style="position:absolute;top:0;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;background:radial-gradient(circle at 20% 50%,rgba(99,102,241,0.15),transparent 50%),radial-gradient(circle at 80% 50%,rgba(236,72,153,0.1),transparent 50%);"></div>
    <div class="container" style="position:relative;z-index:1;text-align:center;">
      <div style="width:80px;height:80px;border-radius:50%;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#818cf8,#f472b6);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin:0 auto 24px;font-size:2.2rem;box-shadow:0 0 40px rgba(99,102,241,0.3);">
        📋
      </div>
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2rem,5vw,3.2rem);font-weight:800;color:white;margin-bottom:20px;">
        AI Receptionist <span style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#818cf8,#f472b6,#22d3ee);-webkit-background-clip:text;-webkit-text-fill-color:transparent;">Buyer's Guide</span>
      </h1>
      <p style="font-size:1.15rem;color:#cbd5e1;max-width:650px;margin:0 auto;line-height:1.8;">
        5 questions to ask before you buy an AI receptionist for your real estate business. No fluff, just what actually matters.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Guide -->
  <section style="padding:80px 0;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1a0f2e 0%,#2d1b4e 100%);">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:750px;">

      <div style="background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:16px;padding:32px;margin-bottom:40px;">
        <p style="color:#94a3b8;font-size:0.95rem;line-height:1.7;">
          The AI receptionist space is exploding — there are 20+ options and every one claims to be the best. This guide cuts through the noise. These are the 5 questions I ask every agent before recommending a solution.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#64748b;font-size:0.85rem;margin-top:12px;">
          — Luna, Birky Studio
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Q1 -->
      <div style="margin-bottom:48px;">
        <div style="width:44px;height:44px;border-radius:50%;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#6366f1,#818cf8);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:700;color:white;margin-bottom:16px;">1</div>
        <h2 style="color:white;font-size:1.4rem;margin-bottom:12px;">Does it do WhatsApp or just phone calls?</h2>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:12px;">
          This is the #1 question most agents don't ask. In Guatemala (and most of Latin America), WhatsApp is how business happens. Clients message you at 9pm on WhatsApp — not call your office line. If your AI receptionist only handles phone calls, you're still missing 60-70% of your leads.
        </p>
        <div style="background:rgba(16,185,129,0.1);border-left:4px solid #10b981;border-radius:8px;padding:16px 20px;">
          <p style="color:#6ee7b7;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.6;">
            <strong>Look for:</strong> A solution that handles BOTH WhatsApp messages AND phone calls. Bonus if it's the same AI in both channels so the conversation history carries over.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Q2 -->
      <div style="margin-bottom:48px;">
        <div style="width:44px;height:44px;border-radius:50%;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#6366f1,#818cf8);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:700;color:white;margin-bottom:16px;">2</div>
        <h2 style="color:white;font-size:1.4rem;margin-bottom:12px;">Is it bilingual (or just English)?</h2>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:12px;">
          If your market has any Spanish-speaking clients, a monolingual AI receptionist will lose you business. The AI needs to switch between English and Spanish naturally — not just have a separate Spanish mode you toggle manually.
        </p>
        <div style="background:rgba(16,185,129,0.1);border-left:4px solid #10b981;border-radius:8px;padding:16px 20px;">
          <p style="color:#6ee7b7;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.6;">
            <strong>Look for:</strong> AI that auto-detects language and responds in the same language. A client should be able to message in Spanish and get a Spanish answer without any setup.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Q3 -->
      <div style="margin-bottom:48px;">
        <div style="width:44px;height:44px;border-radius:50%;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#6366f1,#818cf8);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:700;color:white;margin-bottom:16px;">3</div>
        <h2 style="color:white;font-size:1.4rem;margin-bottom:12px;">Is it trained on YOUR business — or generic?</h2>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:12px;">
          Most AI receptionist services give you a generic script. They ask "How can I help you?" and don't know your listings, your pricing, your hours, or your specific services. A custom-trained AI knows what properties you have, where they're located, how much they cost, and what makes your business unique.
        </p>
        <div style="background:rgba(16,185,129,0.1);border-left:4px solid #10b981;border-radius:8px;padding:16px 20px;">
          <p style="color:#6ee7b7;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.6;">
            <strong>Look for:</strong> A setup process where they actually learn about your business. If they just flip a switch and hand it over, your clients will get generic answers that don't convert.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Q4 -->
      <div style="margin-bottom:48px;">
        <div style="width:44px;height:44px;border-radius:50%;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#6366f1,#818cf8);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:700;color:white;margin-bottom:16px;">4</div>
        <h2 style="color:white;font-size:1.4rem;margin-bottom:12px;">What's the REAL monthly cost?</h2>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:12px;">
          Some services look cheap at first glance but charge per minute, per call, or per lead. Others have a flat monthly fee but limit how many calls you can take. And some have a one-time setup plus a small variable cost. Here's what the market actually looks like:
        </p>
        <div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:20px 0;">
          <table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:0.9rem;">
            <thead>
              <tr style="background:rgba(99,102,241,0.3);">
                <th style="padding:12px 16px;color:white;font-weight:600;text-align:left;">Model</th>
                <th style="padding:12px 16px;color:white;font-weight:600;text-align:left;">Setup</th>
                <th style="padding:12px 16px;color:white;font-weight:600;text-align:left;">Monthly</th>
                <th style="padding:12px 16px;color:white;font-weight:600;text-align:left;">WhatsApp</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);">
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:white;">BirkyStudio (Text)</td>
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:#cbd5e1;">$297</td>
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:#6ee7b7;">$0*</td>
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:#6ee7b7;">✅</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);">
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:white;">BirkyStudio (Voice)</td>
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:#cbd5e1;">$550</td>
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:#cbd5e1;">~$30-50**</td>
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:#6ee7b7;">✅</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);">
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:white;">Goodcall</td>
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:#cbd5e1;">$0</td>
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:#cbd5e1;">$59</td>
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:#ef4444;">❌</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);">
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:white;">Smith.ai</td>
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:#cbd5e1;">$0</td>
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:#cbd5e1;">from $240</td>
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:#ef4444;">❌</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);">
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:white;">Dialpad</td>
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:#cbd5e1;">$0</td>
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:#cbd5e1;">from $23</td>
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:#6ee7b7;">✅</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:white;">Loman AI</td>
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:#cbd5e1;">$0</td>
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:#cbd5e1;">from $99</td>
                <td style="padding:12px 16px;color:#ef4444;">❌</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p style="color:#64748b;font-size:0.78rem;line-height:1.6;">
          * Text-only. Client provides their own OpenRouter API key (~$2-15/mo usage).<br>
          ** Voice receptionist: client pays Vapi directly for call minutes.
        </p>
        <div style="background:rgba(16,185,129,0.1);border-left:4px solid #10b981;border-radius:8px;padding:16px 20px;margin-top:16px;">
          <p style="color:#6ee7b7;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.6;">
            <strong>Look for:</strong> Total cost over 12 months, not just the monthly price. A $59/mo service costs $708/year. A $297 one-time setup with $40/mo variable costs is $777/year — nearly identical, but the one-time option is cheaper if you scale.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Q5 -->
      <div style="margin-bottom:48px;">
        <div style="width:44px;height:44px;border-radius:50%;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#6366f1,#818cf8);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:700;color:white;margin-bottom:16px;">5</div>
        <h2 style="color:white;font-size:1.4rem;margin-bottom:12px;">Who answers when the AI doesn't know?</h2>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:12px;">
          Every AI hits a question it can't answer. What happens then? Some services just say "I don't know" and the call ends. Others transfer to voicemail. The best ones transfer to YOU in real-time so you can pick up and save the lead. Make sure you know the escalation path before you buy.
        </p>
        <div style="background:rgba(16,185,129,0.1);border-left:4px solid #10b981;border-radius:8px;padding:16px 20px;">
          <p style="color:#6ee7b7;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.6;">
            <strong>Look for:</strong> Real-time call transfer to your phone. Not voicemail, not "call back later" — actual forwarding so you can pick up and close the deal.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Bottom line -->
      <div style="background:rgba(99,102,241,0.1);border:1px solid rgba(99,102,241,0.25);border-radius:16px;padding:40px;margin-top:48px;text-align:center;">
        <h2 style="color:white;font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:16px;">The Bottom Line</h2>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:8px;">
          The right AI receptionist saves you 10+ hours a week and never misses a lead. The wrong one is an expensive voicemail machine.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:24px;">
          If you want a custom-trained AI that handles WhatsApp + phone calls + transfers to you + speaks English and Spanish — <strong style="color:white;">that's exactly what we build.</strong>
        </p>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary" style="font-size:1.05rem;padding:16px 32px;">
          Talk to Luna About Your Setup →
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>